Panda and Koala Children’s Charity Concert
《熊猫与考拉》儿童慈善音乐会
In 2021, the Panda and Koala Children’s Charity Concert was held to raise funds for the giant pandas at Adelaide Zoo. The name of the event reflected its cultural meaning: the panda symbolised China, while the koala symbolised Australia. Through this child-centred charity project, we hoped to plant the seeds of friendship between China and Australia in the hearts of young children.
The event combined children’s musical performances with a handmade craft charity sale, encouraging young participants to contribute to wildlife protection through music, creativity, and community action.
A special feature of this event was that all performers, including the hosts, were children. Young participants not only sang and performed on stage, but also took responsibility for presenting the concert to the audience. This gave children a meaningful opportunity to build confidence, communication skills, stage experience, and a sense of social responsibility.
The charity sale also featured handmade items created by children themselves, including paintings, keyrings, and other small craft works. Through making and selling their own creative pieces, the children were able to take part in fundraising in a direct and personal way.
A total of $1,575 was raised through the concert and children’s handmade craft sale. The funds were donated to support the giant pandas at Adelaide Zoo and were presented with the assistance of Ms Lyn Write, former President of the Australia China Friendship Society.
This event reflected our belief that music education can go beyond the classroom and the stage. Through performance, creativity, charitable giving, and cross-cultural friendship, children can learn empathy, environmental awareness, community participation, and the joy of helping others.
《熊猫与考拉》儿童慈善音乐会
2021年，《熊猫与考拉》儿童慈善音乐会举办，旨在为阿德莱德动物园的大熊猫筹集善款。本次活动名称具有特别的文化意义：熊猫象征中国，考拉象征澳大利亚。我们希望通过这个以儿童为中心的慈善项目，从小在孩子们心中播下澳中友好的种子。
本次活动结合儿童音乐表演与儿童手工艺品义卖，鼓励孩子们通过音乐、创造力和社区行动参与野生动物保护。
本次活动的一个重要特色是，所有演员，包括主持人，全部由孩子担任。孩子们不仅在舞台上演唱和表演，也承担了向观众介绍和串联音乐会的角色。这为他们提供了建立自信、锻炼表达能力、积累舞台经验以及培养社会责任感的宝贵机会。
慈善义卖部分也全部由孩子们亲手制作作品，包括画作、钥匙扣及其他小型手工艺品。通过亲自创作、展示和义卖自己的作品，孩子们以直接而真实的方式参与了筹款行动。
本次音乐会及儿童手工艺品义卖共筹得 1,575澳元。善款用于支持阿德莱德动物园的大熊猫项目，并由 澳中友好协会前会长 Lyn Write 女士 协助转交。
这场活动体现了我们的理念：音乐教育不应只停留在课堂与舞台之中。通过表演、创作、慈善行动与跨文化友谊，孩子们能够学习同理心、环保意识、社区参与，以及帮助他人的快乐。
Aged Care Community Performance
养老院公益演出
On 20 April 2026, South Australian International Musicians Association presented an aged care community performance at Southern Cross Care Carmelite Health & Fitness Centre.
This performance brought live music into an aged care community, creating a warm and meaningful space for elderly residents, young performers, families, and community members to connect through music.
During the performance, many residents watched the children with gentle smiles. Some were deeply moved and became emotional as they listened. These moments reminded us that music can reach people beyond words, bringing comfort, memory, companionship, and dignity.
For the young performers, this was also a powerful experience. They felt respected, seen, and valued by the elderly audience. Through this performance, the children learned that music is not only for competitions or formal stages. Music can also be an act of care, kindness, and human connection.
This event reflected our commitment to bringing music into the wider community and creating opportunities for young people to serve others through their artistic gifts.
